Overview
********

‘anki-gt’ is an Emacs client Anki that uses the AnkiConnect
(https://git.sr.ht/~foosoft/anki-connect) add-on.  It provides a
mu4e-style browser over your Anki collection: a decks buffer, a cards
buffer, a notes buffer, and a preview pane or the raw fields as a
two-column table.  Standard search operators (Anki's own query syntax)
are supported via ‘s’ (search), ‘/’ (narrow), and ‘\’ (widen).

   Actions that need Anki's own UI (edit a note, open a card in the
browser) are one keystroke away.


File: anki-gt.info,  Node: Requirements,  Next: Installation,  Prev: Overview,  Up: Top

Requirements
************

   • Emacs 27.1 or newer.
   • Anki running with the AnkiConnect
     (https://ankiweb.net/shared/info/2055492159) add-on installed and
     reachable at ‘http://127.0.0.1:8765’ by default.


