Connection
==========

   • ‘anki-gt-endpoint’ (default ‘http://127.0.0.1:8765’) -
     AnkiConnect's HTTP address.
   • ‘anki-gt-api-key’ (default ‘nil’) - set if your AnkiConnect
     requires an API key.
   • ‘anki-gt-request-timeout’ (default 10) - seconds to wait for a
     response.

   Verify connectivity with ‘M-x anki-gt-check-connection’.


File: anki-gt.info,  Node: Ruby (furigana) display,  Next: Raise Anki after a jump,  Prev: Connection,  Up: Configuration

Ruby (furigana) display
=======================

‘anki-gt-show-ruby’ (default ‘t’) controls whether readings are rendered
inline as ‘kanji[reading]’.  Toggle at runtime with ‘r’ in any anki-gt
buffer.  To default off:

     (setq anki-gt-show-ruby nil)


File: anki-gt.info,  Node: Raise Anki after a jump,  Next: Audio playback,  Prev: Ruby (furigana) display,  Up: Configuration

Raise Anki after a jump
=======================

AnkiConnect's GUI actions do not raise Anki's window on their own.  Set
‘anki-gt-raise-anki-function’ to a no-argument function that brings Anki
forward.  A shipped macOS helper uses osascript:

     (setq anki-gt-raise-anki-function #'anki-gt-raise-anki-macos)

   Other operating systems will require a similar function.


File: anki-gt.info,  Node: Audio playback,  Next: Preview and list buffers,  Prev: Raise Anki after a jump,  Up: Configuration

Audio playback
==============

‘anki-gt-preview-audio-command’ is auto-detected from ‘afplay’ (macOS),
‘mpv’, then ‘ffplay’.  Override to force a specific binary, or set to
‘nil’ to disable audio playback entirely.


File: anki-gt.info,  Node: Preview and list buffers,  Prev: Audio playback,  Up: Configuration

Preview and list buffers
========================

   • ‘anki-gt-preview-default-view’ (‘preview’ | ‘fields’): starting
     view for a freshly-opened preview buffer.  ‘TAB’ toggles at
     runtime.
   • ‘anki-gt-preview-window-side’ (default ‘right’) and
     ‘anki-gt-preview-window-width’ (default 0.5): where and how wide
     the preview side-window is placed.
   • ‘anki-gt-cards-limit’ (default 500): cards fetched per batch.  ‘M’
     loads the next batch.
   • ‘anki-gt-cards-deck-width’ (default 28) and
     ‘anki-gt-cards-field-width’ (default 30): column widths in the
     cards buffer.


