Info manual
***********

The Info version of this README (‘anki-gt.info’) and its ‘dir’ entry
live at the package root, following the multi-file ELPA convention.
When installed via ‘package.el’ (from an ELPA-style archive or a
‘package-install-file’ on a tarball), Emacs adds the package's content
directory to ‘Info-directory-list’ automatically and ‘C-h i’ lists the
manual under ‘Emacs’.

   For installs that bypass ‘package.el’ (raw ‘:load-path’, git
submodule, straight.el without info handling), point Info at the package
directory once in your config:

     (with-eval-after-load 'info
       (info-initialize)
       (add-to-list 'Info-directory-list
                    (file-name-directory (locate-library "anki-gt"))))

   To rebuild the Info files after editing ‘README.org’:

     make info

   Requires ‘makeinfo’ and ‘install-info’ in ‘PATH’.  Both
‘anki-gt.info’ and ‘dir’ are checked in.


